.TH PKIT 1 "April 2026" "pkit 0.1.2" "General Commands Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBpkit\fR \- A Python project CLI utility base project powered by npkg.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkit
[\fB-f\fR \fIfile\fR | \fB--file\fR \fIfile\fR=\fIpyproject.toml\fR]
     [\fB-q\fR | \fB--quiet\fR] [\fB-v\fR | \fB--verbose\fR] [\fB--trace\fR]
     [\fB--telemetry\fR] [\fB--layout\fR \fIlayout\fR=\fI1up\fR]
     [\fB--no-emoji\fR] [\fB--diff\fR \fI{2up|lines}\fR=\fI2up\fR]
     [\fB-V\fR | \fB--version\fR]
     <command> [args...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
For the full user guide, design notes, and rationale, see:
.PP
https://tracecutter.github.io/npkg/
.PP
Built with Sphinx and hosted on GitHub Pages.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -f, --file \fIfile\fR
Project configuration file. (default: \fIpyproject.toml\fR)

.TP
.B -q, --quiet
Suppress output.

.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Verbose output.

.TP
.B --trace
Enable trace instrumentation.

.TP
.B --telemetry
Enable telemetry instrumentation.

.TP
.B --layout \fIlayout\fR
Output layout. (default: \fI1up\fR)

.TP
.B --emoji, --no-emoji
Enable emoji prefixes in output. (default: \fItrue\fR)

.TP
.B --diff \fI{2up|lines}\fR
Diff output format. (default: \fI2up\fR)

.TP
.B -V, --version
Show the version and exit.

.SH COMMANDS
.PD 0
.TP
.B help
Display help for pkit or a named subcommand.
.TP
.B sub
Minimal kitchen sink demonstrating core Click patterns.
.PD 1v

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PKIT_CONFIG
Path to an alternative configuration file. Overrides the default
\fIpyproject.toml\fR location.

.SH FILES
.TP
\f[CR]pyproject.toml\f[R]
Project configuration file (PEP 621).
This is the authoritative source of project metadata, version information, and dependency declarations.
.TP
Project source directory
The package source tree inspected by \f[CR]pfig\f[R] when analysing imports, dependency intent, and packaging layout.
.TP
\f[CR]pfig_dist/\f[R]
Default output directory for documentation artifacts generated by \f[CR]pfig docs\f[R], including man pages and other render targets.

.SH EXIT STATUS
The \fBpkit\fR command exits with status 0 on success and a non-zero value if an error occurs.

.SH EXAMPLES
List declared dependencies:
.IP
.EX
pfig deps
.EE
.PP
Add a runtime dependency:
.IP
.EX
pfig add requests
.EE
.PP
Add a development dependency:
.IP
.EX
pfig add \-\-dev pytest
.EE
.PP
Bump the project version:
.IP
.EX
pfig bump minor
.EE
.PP
Check project configuration and environment:
.IP
.EX
pfig lint
.EE
.PP
Generate documentation artifacts:
.IP
.EX
pfig docs
.EE
.PP
Inspect a specific field in pyproject.toml:
.IP
.EX
pfig get project.version
.EE

